Make sure SSO accounts are blocked from password for authentication

- Reject password change requests if SAML credentials are available.
- Atomically remove the stored password hash when assigning a SAML identity in both Cassandra and PostgreSQL. Unlinking SAML does not restore the removed password, so password recovery is required. (Rationale: SAML identity and password authentication are mutually exclusive, and passwords should only be stored when needed.)
